<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashot II of Armenia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/929">929</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Ashot II the Iron, Ashot Yerkat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashot II, called Yerkat, 'the Iron', was king of Bagratid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> from 914 to 929. Son of Smbat I, who had been executed by the Sajid emir Yusuf, he fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sajid-dynasty">Sajids</a> and rival Armenian princes for years with Byzantine help and restored royal authority. The Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> recognised him as 'king of kings' in 922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashot-ii-of-armenia.jpg" alt="Ashot II of Armenia" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ohan Gaidzakian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashot_Yerkat.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
